    "observations": [
      {
        "profile": "squid-approach-phone",
        "result": "Improved",
        "detail": "At 390px, the contextual action hint is confined to the right action bank instead of crossing the whole squid. It restores most of the central body and paired-fin silhouette. The lowest tip passes very close to the hint edge in this captured pose, so complete model clearance is not claimed. Controls and important readouts remain legible."
      },
      {
        "profile": "squid-narrow-phone",
        "result": "Improved",
        "detail": "At 320px in this natural empty-hint pose, paired movement controls reclaim roughly one control row. The entire squid remains visible above the dock; this does not establish clearance for every active hint or pose."
      },
      {
        "profile": "squid-landscape-phone",
        "result": "Corrected and accepted",
        "detail": "At 844x390, the responsive narrower action bank now starts to the right of the squid and its paired fins. The prior candidate lower-mantle occlusion is gone; all visible buttons remain readable and separated. The overlay-free GL image confirms unchanged model and scene pose."
      },
      {
        "profile": "squid-approach-desktop",
        "result": "Improved and feedback separated",
        "detail": "At 1280px the actual fine pointer uses desktop readouts, keyboard actions and the minimap despite maxTouchPoints 10. The earned First Dive popup now sits above the contextual action hint, so both remain readable. The central squid and reef remain clear. The GL projection changes slightly with the intentional desktop canvas height; scene transforms and camera pose still match."
      }
    ],
